    {
      "@id": "docs/guides/translation-support.md#provenance-1",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Principle: translations are content nodes",
      "prov:value": "An official translation of a content node is persisted **as its own translated\ncontent node within the source content node's directory**. This follows the\nFRBR pattern already argued for in bean `p2en`: a block varies along two axes —\n**format** (`.md`, `.lean`, `.tex`) and **language** — and the translation is an\nExpression of the same Work.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean p2en"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "docs/guides/translation-support.md#provenance-2",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Round-trip QA (bean `ktt2`)",
      "prov:value": "### Round-trip QA (bean `ktt2`)",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean ktt2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "docs/guides/translation-support.md#provenance-3",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Steps",
      "prov:value": "1. **Translation coordinator** identifies content requiring human translation\n   and selects the target locale.\n2. **POT extraction** produces the translatable string set.\n3. **Translation assignment** — the coordinator assigns the POT to a qualified\n   translator (ideally a domain SME for the content area).\n4. **Translation** — the human translator works in their preferred tool\n   (Poedit, Weblate, Crowdin, or directly editing `.po` files). They receive:\n   - The `.pot` file with source strings\n   - Context notes (block kind, chapter title, surrounding content)\n   - A glossary of domain terms with approved translations\n5. **Completeness check** — the coordinator verifies that all `msgid` entries\n   have `msgstr` translations. Partial translations are acceptable but flagged.\n6. **PO injection** — the completed `.po` file is injected to produce\n   translated markdown.\n7. **SME review** — a subject-matter expert (may be the same translator or a\n   different domain expert) reviews the translation for clinical/technical\n   accuracy. This is especially critical for WHO content where terminology\n   precision has policy implications.\n8. **Round-trip QA** — automated back-translation comparison (bean `ktt2`).\n9. **Sign-off** — the reviewer signs off, making the translation official.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean ktt2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "docs/guides/translation-support.md#provenance-4",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Stages",
      "prov:value": "1. **Content authored** — source content exists in the default locale.\n2. **POT extracted** — translatable strings are extracted.\n3. **Translation produced** — agent or human creates PO file + translated `.md`.\n4. **Round-trip QA** — back-translation detects semantic drift (bean `ktt2`).\n5. **Human review gateway** — drift or bad terminology routes to reviewer.\n6. **Sign-off** — human adjudicator marks translation as official.\n7. **Staleness watch** — source changes trigger re-extraction + stale marking.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean ktt2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "docs/guides/translation-support.md#provenance-5",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Work plan",
      "prov:value": "| Phase | Bean | Description | Status |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1. Documentation | (this document) | Consolidated translation reference | ✅ Done |\n| 2. Schema changes | — | Add `lang` to `BlockBase`, `TranslationStatus` schema | Todo |\n| 3. Config support | — | Add `translation` section to `<name>.config.json` | Todo |\n| 4. POT extraction | — | `content/pipeline/pot-extract.ts` | Todo |\n| 5. PO injection | — | `content/pipeline/po-inject.ts` | Todo |\n| 6. MCP tools | — | Register 5 translation tools | Todo |\n| 7. Viewer language switcher | — | Globe icon + locale dropdown | Todo |\n| 8. Kind heading catalogue | — | Replace hardcoded `KIND_HEADING` with i18n map | Todo |\n| 9. Staleness tracking | — | Hash-based change detection | Todo |\n| 10. Sign-off workflow | — | Multi-level sign-off UI + persistence | Todo |\n| 11. Round-trip QA | `ktt2` | Back-translation drift detection | Todo (existing bean) |\n| 12. SMART Base integration | — | Wrap extraction/injection scripts | Todo |\n| 13. BPMN diagram | — | Translation workflow BPMN | Todo |"
    },
